\begin{definition}
\label{def:7-52-extra-2}




A smooth action of $G$ on a finite-dimensional vector space $V$ is linear if each map $x\mapsto g\cdot x$ is linear. A representation $\rho$ induces the linear action $g\cdot x=\rho(g)x$.
\end{definition}
